  NOTE: 30/30 Bonferroni horizons have lambda = inf. Each is calibrated at alpha/H_max = 0.00167, which needs ceil((n+1)(1-alpha/H_max)) <= n calibration points; with n_cal = 400 that is impossible, so the union bound certifies nothing at all here. That is not a bug in the baseline -- it is the cost Eq. (8) is designed to avoid, and it shows up as an infeasible calibration long before it shows up as a merely shorter horizon.
